{"mode":"probe_at_tier","concept":"information-hiding","target_tier":"Understand","content":"No problem — let's start with the word itself before touching the task.

Think of a module as a small box with a control panel on the outside and wiring inside. The course calls the control panel the **interface** (the public contract: the names, types, return values, and errors callers are allowed to rely on) and the wiring the **implementation** (the secret that's free to change).

Given that picture, one question for you: if the interface is what callers are *permitted to assume*, what would go wrong if the control panel showed the caller the exact wiring diagram inside?","format":null,"rubric":null,"concept_tags":null,"sources":["SEBook > designprinciples > Information Hiding > Applying and Evaluating > Summary (https://github.com/tobiasduerschmid/tobiasduerschmid.github.io/blob/24db6bf0d4e4ebfa1331e6c772e1844cbaf2d9aa/SEBook/designprinciples/informationhiding.md)"],"coverage_gap":null}

{"mode":"probe_at_tier","concept":"information-hiding","target_tier":"Understand","content":"No problem — let's build the word "interface" up first, then the task will make more sense.

Think of a module as a unit of work one person or team owns. It has two parts: the **interface**, which is the contract describing *what* the module does, and the **implementation**, the code inside that actually does it.

Quick check on just that distinction: if you're the one *calling* a module, which of those two parts do you actually need to know about — and why do you think the other part is kept away from you?","format":null,"rubric":null,"concept_tags":null,"sources":["SEBook/designprinciples/informationhiding.md — The Anatomy of a Module: Interface and Secret (https://github.com/tobiasduerschmid/tobiasduerschmid.github.io/blob/24db6bf0d4e4ebfa1331e6c772e1844cbaf2d9aa/SEBook/designprinciples/informationhiding.md)","SEBook/designprinciples/informationhiding.md — Interfaces Are Permission to Assume (https://github.com/tobiasduerschmid/tobiasduerschmid.github.io/blob/24db6bf0d4e4ebfa1331e6c772e1844cbaf2d9aa/SEBook/designprinciples/informationhiding.md)"],"coverage_gap":null}

